# Default owner for everything in the repository.
#
# A code owner review is **not** required on `main`, and this comment used to say
# it was — "enforced by branch protection on `main`", next to a ruleset whose
# `require_code_owner_review` is false. That is the defect this repository spends
# itself on, written into its own governance: a sentence describing a control
# nobody applies reads exactly like the control.
#
# It is false on purpose rather than by oversight. One maintainer cannot approve
# their own pull request, so requiring a code owner review here would close the
# only path this repository has to `main`, and the way past it would be the admin
# bypass — scoring two controls while enforcing neither. docs/scorecard.md states
# the trade, what the bypass does allow (merging a held pull request) and what it
# does not (pushing to `main` directly), and what would change all of it: a
# second reviewer, not a setting.
#
# What this file does today: name the reviewer GitHub requests automatically on
# every pull request, and give the drift bot a human to address.
